  {
    "annotations": {
      "description": "Two faults sit behind this rule. A reload failure in the last 15 minutes is a dynamic configuration Traefik read and refused: a Middleware or IngressRoute it cannot resolve. Traefik keeps serving the last good config, so the routes still answer and the log line is the only evidence; read it with kubectl -n kube-system logs deploy/traefik --tail=100. No successful reload for 24 h is the other shape: the provider delivered nothing for a day, which is not normal here (routes change several times an hour), so the watch is dead or the router is stuck mid-build. It does not cover a Helm values file that fails to render, or the /metrics endpoint being unreachable: the first never reaches Traefik, and ScrapeTargetDown owns the second.",
      "summary": "Traefik is not reloading its configuration"
    },
    "condition": "C",
    "data": [
      {
        "datasourceUid": "PBFA97CFB590B2093",
        "model": {
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(traefik_config_reloads_failure_total[15m])) > 0 or (time() - max(traefik_config_last_reload_success)) > 86400",
          "instant": true,
          "intervalMs": 1000,
          "maxDataPoints": 43200,
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        "queryType": "",
        "refId": "A",
